virtpacker (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Sparse-aware disk copies. --no-flatten and the import step now copy disk
    images through `cp --sparse=always --reflink=auto` instead of shutil, so
    holes in a sparse image are no longer expanded to real zeroes.
  * `list` now reports per-domain size on disk (st_blocks-based) alongside the
    apparent size, with a total.
  * Free-space preflight before export and import: the destination filesystem
    is checked against the estimated on-disk bytes (with a small margin) and
    the run aborts early if short. Bypass with --no-space-check.

 -- Bill Prochazka <bprochazka@verostech.com>  Thu, 04 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0000

virtpacker (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * export and import libvirt domains as portable single-directory bundles.
  * disks copied and flattened to standalone qcow2 by default, with
    --no-flatten available (refuses rather than mishandling a backing chain).
  * nvram carried in the bundle; on import the domain switches to UEFI
    firmware autoselection so the host picks its own OVMF or edk2 build.
  * swtpm TPM state handled in two modes: an explicit <backend><source>
    path is read from the domain XML when present (libvirt 10.8 and later),
    otherwise the UUID-derived default directory is used.
  * SELinux contexts restored on import via restorecon, with a semanage
    fcontext rule added for non-standard destination directories.

 -- Bill Prochazka <bprochazka@verostech.com>  Wed, 03 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0000
